# SRG-APP-000835-AU-000300  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must for password-based authentication, update the
# list of passwords on an organization-defined frequency.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000835-AU-000300
group:           V-263575
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   ORGANIZATIONAL
grade:           D
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-004059
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    None: with no password deny list in the product there is nothing for the
                 application to update, and Splunk Enterprise 10.4.2 has no setting
                 expressing an update frequency for such a list. The only scheduled
                 credential behavior the product can be configured with is password
                 expiration (authentication.conf [splunk_auth] expirePasswordDays,
                 expireUserAccounts), which is a different control and is assessed under
                 SRG-APP-000870.

external:        Updating the list on the organization-defined frequency - carried by
                 organizational policy and the process that maintains the list.
external:        Distribution of the updated list to the screening component - carried by
                 the directory service or identity provider where authType is LDAP, SAML,
                 or ProxySSO.

manual_reason:   The requirement is to update a list the product does not hold; no conf key
                 expresses the list or the frequency of its update, so no observed
                 configuration value can decide it. The frequency is organization-defined.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/authentication.conf.spec:437-600 ([splunk_auth];
                 expirePasswordDays at :487 governs password expiration, not a deny list)
finding:         Not a finding against the application: Splunk Enterprise 10.4.2 holds no
                 password deny list and has no setting for its update frequency, so this
                 requirement is carried by organizational policy and by the identity
                 provider that holds the list; this determination is from the perspective
                 of the application layer alone.
